        "answer": "Resets the shared current sequence index to 1, stores the sequence reference, then updates FTUE info using that sequence's first overlay. It does not guard the sequence/overlay table lookups or mark a sequence completed. For CoD.FTUEUtility.SetCurrentSequence, evaluate the displayed formal inputs and captured values. Its writes/requests begin 1042: CoD.FTUEUtility.CurrentSequenceIndex = 1; 1043: CoD.FTUEUtility.CurrentSequenceReference = f46_arg2. The statement contracts below preserve exact arguments, reads/writes, short-circuit tests, loop and return behavior. Rejects a sequence for the wrong required session mode or the skip-first-time dvar. Otherwise it returns true only when the selected storage buffer and named stats field exist and that field equals 0. Missing storage/field returns false. The sequence-info table itself is assumed present by this source. For CoD.FTUEUtility.ShouldS [excerpt; exact source record identified separately]",
